  "recommendations": [
    {
      "mechanism": "Restore case-insensitive constituent relations and input/task context to shared signatures",
      "reason": "Current candidate representation has casefold equality but lacks case-insensitive contains/starts/ends relations, despite upper/lower normalization of proper output constituents being central to 15/16 lost jobs. Official BUSTLE compares these relations and adds task/input signatures. This is an actionable missing observable, not evidence of an irreducible exact collision.",
      "test": "Add six case-insensitive containment directions plus bounded task-input relations for every controller. Rebuild labels from past verified programs, freeze prospective source and compare against explicit heuristic using the same observables. Keep exact source03 result unchanged."
    },
    {
      "mechanism": "Learn priorities of operand-plus-operation-family actions rather than operand membership alone",
      "reason": "Current neural score chooses an operand but cannot choose its transformation; generator spends token, split, slice, replace and number batches in a fixed order. Positive subtree membership is a weak proxy for useful next expansion, and current losses use thousands of invalid interpreter attempts.",
      "test": "Rank (operand observations, prospective operation family) using only parent-child edges in past buyer-accepted ASTs. Do not expose newly generated parent values or target-equality result before its metered execution. Controls receive identical edge labels, action sets and budgets; independent buyer checks remain unchanged. Root edges may teach operators, but final output/root itself must never be a feature. Keep parameter enumeration and multi-child concat accounting explicit."
    }
  ],
